{"title":"2001 Iran NMO (Round 3) Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Iran_NMO_(Round_3)_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10c492116dccb7c0e00af0fcc7f618db9b2d2112.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f: \\mathbb Q\\longrightarrow\\mathbb Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> such that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/5472c970ff1eb6a618a242f092e3c4e1a789cd66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)+f(\\frac1x)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"132\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1f410bceca7a97a723e7018cdc6e8ec7c125a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2f(f(x))=f(2x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_.28credit_to_Bandera.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_(credit_to_Bandera)\">Solution (credit to Bandera)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Iran_NMO_(Round_3)_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution (credit to Bandera)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Claim: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/6/6f6a6d5911c076cfda23f4c4801b9bf02b0a100c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\dfrac{x}{x+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"107\" height=\"36\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd2de0a647eb8c416abdd1ff7a95736dfd79533.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb N$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> be the set of positive integers. Note that the representation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/7/217ce02a3c69a47e9502aa93f5e46c757256b382.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\tfrac x{1+x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"90\" height=\"23\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f40830de530e851999c97c23e10f5c39028f4934.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\tfrac i j,\\;i,\\,j \\in \\mathbb N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"121\" height=\"25\" /> is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/967c36a595e079bf228ea49b6cd68ce4231b55a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(\\tfrac i j)=\\tfrac i{i+j}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"91\" height=\"25\" /> It is easy to see that the function specified at the answer satisfies both equations: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdcf32ee97910188d9de8f063cc42ec28be93c13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(\\tfrac i j)+f(\\tfrac j i)=\\tfrac i{i+j}+\\tfrac j{i+j}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"224\" height=\"26\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/8/87867311cdf1b0cffa6dabaf5d909213a6e959fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2f(f(\\tfrac i j))=2f(\\tfrac i{i+j})=2\\,\\tfrac i{2i+j}=\\tfrac {2i}{2i+j}=f(\\tfrac {2i}j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"343\" height=\"25\" /> for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/d/0adacbbf5e50f2072f72230d2d3cefe17edc6c98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i,\\,j \\in \\mathbb N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />. Let's prove that, conversely, any function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> that satisfies the equations has the said form. For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13160bc6af4904ad40a3e6f6e08c8708570ff78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\in \\mathbb N, n \\ge 2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" /> denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c541366d656f08a8e5006251ae56f0549b9999de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb Q_n=\\left\\{\\,\\frac i j \\;\\middle\\vert\\, i+j=n,\\,i,j \\in \\mathbb N \\right\\}\\!,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"251\" height=\"45\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/4/4642a0bc1ace636f52876b28ad8d48205f8a1c6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\;\\mathbb I_n=\\{1,2\\dots,n-1\\}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"20\" /> Also let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a75c05390a4c48ac208777a8f7a0e2e47fa15ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E=\\left\\{x \\in \\mathbb Q^+ \\;\\middle\\vert\\, f(x)=\\tfrac x{1+x}\\right\\}\\!.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"229\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p>Plan of proof (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> below is any number from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb54ebd5370e081c6ada1f08cc679c663b32a590.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb Q^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is any number from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd2de0a647eb8c416abdd1ff7a95736dfd79533.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb N$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />)\n1. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/3/ce383d9c9a0a2579d370938681421b46d0b6cd78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)+f\\left(\\tfrac 1 x \\right)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"134\" height=\"24\" />\n2. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1f410bceca7a97a723e7018cdc6e8ec7c125a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2f(f(x))=f(2x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" />\n3. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea71c7afa9be9069e7f07a38efb818ee155fde25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb Q_2 \\subset E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />.\n4. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/d/5dd8a82d3624747d1fc78ddfbfb7eff45796a549.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\cup_{m=2}^{n-1} \\,\\mathbb Q_m \\subset E) \\implies \\mathbb Q_n \\subset E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"237\" height=\"21\" />.\n5. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4cecee88f8b68b55422edfd28f51b74a6dda7b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E=\\mathbb Q^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Details\n1.A Given.\n2.A Given.\n3.A 1<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/6/c36f7a9116651f076984b66f55cb64249f8e0458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x \\gets 1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />&#160;: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/e/5ded2a15efb6c77bcc87ba43e78130026277be14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)+f(1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f78024951b6e53a606210bda5066f17eef76ba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=\\tfrac 1 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"71\" height=\"23\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/a/a5a2aca7b4cf1e27fe3095a020653e46fb5cd78f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, consisting of a single point, is contained inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n4.A Suppose the premise is true for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1e2533d6abdb11a9a1626c0240fab1a9200fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f6c9b5d4313025ece38b1a38e2752491b185ed5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb Q_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> is a finite set consisting of the elements <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/5/eb53ee48fa883fc3f0e2b0e323aa15c7e8792c39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q_i=\\tfrac i {n-i},\\,i \\in \\mathbb I_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"123\" height=\"24\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b8928b4368ae1a27d1079645acd5c5668bc3868c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i=nf(q_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" />. We need to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/ecc1b91f70f2d52daad337b3905827beef2261ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(q_i)=f(\\tfrac i{n-i})=\\tfrac i n \\iff x_i=i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"253\" height=\"24\" /> for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/8/3f84a48d649a0ed04b697ff5144571babc6bdcc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\in \\mathbb I_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" />. Define the map <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0619a08cbece24a1d149b1f07ac6d4be23c8d210.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h \\colon \\mathbb I_n \\to \\mathbb I_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/9172fd6093e9c527cd891e1f6f7f8e693a079fea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(i)=\\begin{cases}2i,&amp; i&lt;\\tfrac n 2\\\\n-i,&amp; i \\ge \\tfrac n 2\\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"177\" height=\"55\" />. Now take any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/8/3f84a48d649a0ed04b697ff5144571babc6bdcc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\in \\mathbb I_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/8/0d82ecbff560aee657a3643f8708cc6b0fc6ef86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i&lt;\\tfrac n 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"45\" height=\"20\" />, then 2<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/8/b4889afd11c48acd0b392eb49836c451170c3f26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x \\gets \\tfrac i{n-2i}]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"84\" height=\"24\" />&#160;: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/c/48cd0822c8a31cc14d1e6100dbd0f9a9e5e7609b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2f(f(\\tfrac i{n-2i}))=f(\\tfrac {2i}{n-2i})=f(q_{2i})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"247\" height=\"24\" />. Clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/f/56fa559d3d6bd5101bea14a523a5e92c39130895.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac i{n-2i} \\in \\mathbb Q_{n-i} \\subseteq \\cup_{m=2}^{n-1} \\,\\mathbb Q_m \\subset E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"230\" height=\"24\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/d/e8d8577821206d525fdd37afb7e664445f5cd224.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(\\tfrac i{n-2i})=\\tfrac i{n-i}=q_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"150\" height=\"24\" /> and so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/f/caf1a04fc87f3b847815cdcbe29b8754260f1843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2f(q_i)=f(q_{2i})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />. After multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, this becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a62032eb608b3319fd26977ecaf380a9036fde9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x_i=x_{2i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"17\" />, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/e/bfe3b5d5a199ad29aa068bc7cd7b2d90434af90e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{h(i)}=2x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"85\" height=\"19\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc95819bf8da32f6cf10be85b89c5e0e62cdcd76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\ge \\tfrac n 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"45\" height=\"20\" />, then 1<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/4/424f42af7ccb241b1e9112890c2e94f9c004eee3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x \\gets \\tfrac i{n-i}]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"78\" height=\"24\" />&#160;: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/0/ea0738ae1b28a75b8479abfeb41c137f85aa299e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(\\tfrac i{n-i})+f(\\tfrac {n-i}i)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"162\" height=\"24\" />, that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/9/2896a3d7c10971ce0ddac2f4094c299bffaeb1ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(q_i)+f(q_{n-i})=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df60d46230aaab6eefc97c3759bf32477108f860.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i+x_{n-i}=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/4/e44ecd049bd3d2ad610c63a2f247991b3acd8231.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{h(i)}=n-x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" />. In both cases, we have a linear relation between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5b2d2078fa4298a072118cf2e5a8ed2de083195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{h(i)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"36\" height=\"15\" />. Combining these relations for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/8/3f84a48d649a0ed04b697ff5144571babc6bdcc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\in \\mathbb I_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" /> we get a system of equations in the variables <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea2949f6c79ee43787e0deac1e504792f941b17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i, i \\in \\mathbb I_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />. It's not hard to see that this system, consisting only of equations of kind <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a62032eb608b3319fd26977ecaf380a9036fde9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x_i=x_{2i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df60d46230aaab6eefc97c3759bf32477108f860.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i+x_{n-i}=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" />, has a solution that we need: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc0179b08acea43122172760fca6790651d4126c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall i \\in \\mathbb I_n \\colon x_i=i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"17\" />. To prove that this system doesn't have other solutions, take any initial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/8/4b801578ccb4f48e5c899d5a767a35493bc00b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_0 \\in \\mathbb I_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f450c339187edc2c685d8e997deb76ef50697db4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=x_{i_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />. We have a trivial equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6e608efc23d5b79546ddece0fc8a647197bd7cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i_0}=a_0x+b_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"19\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5b68cf5383f735a56d3913666d052b60282f5e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=1,\\,b_0=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />. For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cec8d8345a476b8ca52d2e4c32d712dd5ed7169f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/c/7ac19472d8c8cbf8ff3d7780fb51d208c106c397.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_{m+1}=h(i_m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" /> and if we already have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/e/03e88e3bd636b35190386dc30542f490cef5eb42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i_m}=a_mx+b_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"19\" />, then we can add a new equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/4/3249d418d23609c542138c050996b388e974923e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i_{m+1}}=a_{m+1}x+b_{m+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"176\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/f/a1f96000a04b73f591a9aa67bb0b96c824382ce5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{m+1}=2a_m,\\,b_{m+1}=2b_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"199\" height=\"18\" /> in case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/7/4a7b7d8f8724b08329971a564f05512ec95d024a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_m &lt; \\tfrac n 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/3/283bb61dcc180eb0943f3b441973e2b9c88b4963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{m+1}=-a_m,\\,b_{m+1}=n-b_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"228\" height=\"18\" /> otherwise. We get an infinite sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8450c8383e7792c69f21b11c85d3632d931e6e46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i_m)_{m \\ge 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" /> with a corresponding equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/e/03e88e3bd636b35190386dc30542f490cef5eb42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i_m}=a_mx+b_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"19\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. Owing to the finiteness of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/f/fef719b06159d56a348ec764d6a55248938f6abd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb I_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" />, this sequence repeats, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/f/8af414e58ddb2ec655f4b2f4d3f794dcd039190a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_p=i_q,\\,p&lt;q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"107\" height=\"19\" /> be the first time when it happens. This implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/3/873f1359aec21b9a78d4db01bf43f04902c86d85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_px+b_p=x_{i_p}=x_{i_q}=a_qx+b_q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"250\" height=\"20\" />, but this equation in the unknown <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> has only a single solution due to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/3/4f311af316c81d4446bb5a9be7f5d41a6ac4aef4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_p \\ne a_q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" />. Indeed, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/8/578d1f97df9d68485d18f5a76593fd4e0efcc43b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_m|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"20\" />, which is initially <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, never decreases and doubles at least one time in any two consecutive steps because the second case of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e07ccde14bf8f9909e2dffb32cc376e7d334db58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"33\" height=\"20\" /> is never applied twice in a row, except <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3cea2707dbb96920f29c1684a283aa78a2a8ca38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i_m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"20\" /> cycles on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/0/b5000b347576a9307e19f650fa670e91aacb6990.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_p=i_{p+1}=\\tfrac n 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" />. So either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/5/c15dd6c1e8adeaad39a225bb85853a76f2585755.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q&gt;p+1 \\implies |a_q|&gt;|a_p|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"203\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aee36458089843d8d626f14dbe3bc8e04f8b01ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=p+1 \\implies a_q=-a_p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"197\" height=\"19\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f450c339187edc2c685d8e997deb76ef50697db4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=x_{i_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> is uniquely determined by the system.\n5.A We use induction on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/0/d6021765633e2f990d1eb66f085052f46e1cd932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb Q_n \\subset E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" /> for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317096889b84df0b72bf69ceb4c82208305f1b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />. 3 gives the base case, 4 gives the inductive step. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/b/6db582d406e2f7735bb4c293c74e0d6c2c640fdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb Q^+=\\cup_{n=2}^{\\infty} \\,\\mathbb Q_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/8/538f75261deeae5b0775de8f9885674b5b215d36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb Q^+ \\subseteq E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" /> and obviously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a52717d6bde067156792faf32f37bb9956accaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E \\subseteq \\mathbb Q^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017195359\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 296/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18241/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:34903:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017195359 and revision id 270556. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}